You classify ONE article for a research brief. You do NOT count, date, or route anything — those are already computed and must be copied through verbatim.

DOMAIN: ${config.data.topic}
${config.data.domainHint}

ARTICLE
url: ${input.data.url}
title: ${input.data.title}
opening: ${input.data.extract}

Assign EXACTLY ONE category, using one of these strings verbatim:
${config.data.categories}

If none fits, use "unrelated". Prefer an existing category over inventing a near-duplicate.

Then distil the knowledge this page carries, from its text only: `summary` = two sentences (under 300 characters) on the angle it takes and who it is for; `keyPoints` = 3 to 5 short, concrete points (under 120 characters each: values, steps, claims) a writer could use later. Keep every string on one line with double quotes escaped — a truncated or malformed object costs a second round trip.

Everything you need is in this prompt — there is nothing to look up, so do NOT call THINK and do not query anything. Deliver by calling DONE exactly once, on your FIRST iteration, passing EXACTLY this JSON object as the value of its `message` parameter (the object itself, no markdown fences, no sentence about it):
{"url":"${input.data.url}","recency":"${input.data.recency}","publishedAt":"${input.data.publishedAt}","title":"${input.data.title}","blobUrn":"${input.data.blobUrn}","briefId":"${input.data.briefId}","sourceType":"${input.data.sourceType}","category":"...","summary":"...","keyPoints":["...","...","..."],"confidence":"high|medium|low"}

Copy url, recency, publishedAt, title, blobUrn, briefId and sourceType EXACTLY as given. Do not recompute or omit them. blobUrn is the ONLY pointer to the stored full text: this lane's answer object REPLACES the token, so a field you leave out is lost for good. Your whole reply is one tool call: {"reasoning":"...","tool":"DONE","params":{"message":{ ...the object above... }}}. DONE is the only channel that returns an answer — prose outside it is discarded and the run is wasted.

You are the staff writer for this investigation. One accepted article task has been assembled into the packet below; write the publish-ready draft.

TOPIC: ${config.data.topic}
${config.data.domainHint}

THE ASSIGNMENT
title: ${input.data.title}
why it was accepted: ${input.data.rationale}
category: ${input.data.gapCategory}

THE COMPETITOR PIECE THIS MUST BEAT (${input.data.competitorUrl}):
${input.data.competitorText}

RELATED ARTICLES ALREADY ON THE OWNER'S SITE (link them with relative paths like /slug/ where they genuinely help the reader; never repeat their content): ${input.data.relatedOwnSlugs}

Write 1100-1500 words of practical, publish-ready markdown:
- Open with the reader's actual problem, not a definition.
- Deliver what the rationale says the competitor stops short of — that is the whole point of this assignment.
- Structure with ## and ### headings; use tables or numbered steps where they beat prose.
- Concrete values over vague advice. Plain language. No filler intros, no 'in conclusion'.
- Do NOT copy or closely paraphrase the competitor's sentences; write from understanding.
- Include a short FAQ (3 questions) at the end if the topic invites one.

Everything you need is in this prompt — do NOT call THINK and do not query anything. Deliver by calling DONE exactly once, on your FIRST iteration, passing EXACTLY this JSON object as the value of its `message` parameter (the object itself, no markdown fences around it):
